        "raw": "<p>Here&#39;s a solo scenario I wrote for SotM:</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p align=\"CENTER\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><u>The Next Evolution</u></p><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><i>History</i>: After his father fell at the hands of <b>Baron Blade</b>, <b>Legacy</b> set out to destroy the evil battle suit that <b>Blade</b> had used. <b>Baron Blade</b> rallied his troops, but given <b>Legacy&#39;s</b> new impenetrable skin, he might have bitten off more than he could chew...</p><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;</p><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><i>Setup:</i></p><ul><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\">This is a 1-person scenario. Use <b>Baron Blade</b> (Vengeful Mad Scientist), America&#39;s Finest <b>Legacy</b>, and the <b>Mobile Defense Platform</b>.</p></li><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\">Remove &ldquo;Heroic Interception,&rdquo; &ldquo;Bolster Allies,&rdquo; and &ldquo;Lead from the Front&rdquo; from <b>Legacy&#39;s </b>Deck.</p></li><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\">Remove &ldquo;Mobile Defense Platform&rdquo; (The battle takes place <i>inside </i>it), &ldquo;Elemental Redistributor&rdquo; (A worthless weapon against <b>Legacy,</b> the <b>Baron</b> wouldn&#39;t bother using it), and &ldquo;Hasten Doom&rdquo; (<b>Blade</b> hasn&#39;t invented the Anti-Legacy serum yet) from <b>Baron Blade&#39;s</b> deck.</p></li><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><b>Legacy</b> starts play with &ldquo;The Legacy Ring,&rdquo; &ldquo;Motivational Charge,&rdquo; and &ldquo;Fortitude&rdquo; in play.</p></li><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><b>Baron Blade</b> starts with only 25 HP on his &ldquo;Vengeful Made Scientist&rdquo; side (this is an older version of his battle suit).</p></li><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%;\">Otherwise, the game works normally.</p></li></ul><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;</p><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><i>End of Game:</i> Whenever one side is incapacitated, the other side wins.</p><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;</p><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\"><i>Balance:</i></p><ul><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%;\">If you&#39;re finding the scenario too easy, start without &ldquo;Fortitude&rdquo; in play, or with a &ldquo;Blade Battalion&rdquo; in play.</p></li><li><p align=\"LEFT\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0in; line-height: 150%\">If you&#39;re finding the scenario too hard, let <b>Legacy</b> go first, then play normally.</p></li></ul>",
